WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.320
- [Narrator] Let's say you wanted to buy

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:03.630
a popular Rolex Daytona watch,

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:07.080
a new one would cost you $14,800.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:10.110
But if you wanted to buy a used
version of this same watch,

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.620
you might need to pay over $38,000.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.340
So why are people spending
more money to get a used Rolex?

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.980
- If you use your watch
primarily for telling time,

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.780
then we're not of the same mindset.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.270
- [Narrator] Here's why the
used watch market is booming,

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.970
and what Rolex is doing
to get in on the action.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:29.971
This is the economics of used Rolexes.

00:00:29.971 --> 00:00:32.340
(gentle music)

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.460
Experts suggest that it takes
about a year to make a Rolex,

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:38.820
and wait list for new watches
can last months to years,

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:39.780
and because of that.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.820
- These days you can't
walk into any Rolex store

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:44.490
any Rolex dealer and just
get any watch that you want.

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:47.190
For the past few years,
as demand has increased,

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:50.520
Rolex has not been able to
keep up with that demand,

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.260
their production just can't match

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.060
the number of people that want a Rolex.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:57.240
If you've got 10, $20,000 to
burn, you really wanna watch,

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:58.890
you're probably gonna
go to the resale market

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:01.620
because the watch that you want
is gonna be available there,

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.740
and so the prices on the
resale market have then gone up

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:07.230
because there's more people
going to that market.

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:08.880
- [Narrator] 29% of collectors

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.980
reported paying more than retail price

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.900
for their most recent pre-owned watch,

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.570
according to a report from
Boston Consulting Group.

00:01:15.570 --> 00:01:18.570
And 40% said that one of their top reasons

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:21.120
was that they were able to
avoid long waiting lists

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.980
in the firsthand market,

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.860
this has created a boom
in the secondary market.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.730
Pre-owned watch sales
reached 22 billion in 2021.

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:32.400
The used sector is actually growing faster

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.600
than the primary market,

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:34.830
and for some people

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.350
used watches are worth more than new ones

00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.930
that's because some rare
styles are more desirable,

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:43.740
or because Rolex has discontinued
certain models and colors.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.780
- An older model Rolex can have a patina,

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:46.950
it can have some wear marks,

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:49.440
and so those kind of personal details,

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.000
those kind of personal age marks,

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.770
those are things that
collectors might want.

00:01:52.770 --> 00:01:54.510
There is also a bragging rights thing

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:57.120
where if you have a Rolex
from the '70s or the '80s,

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.310
you're able to say it's from this era,

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:01.950
it's, you know, 20, 30
years older than I am

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.350
and that is just kind of
cool to collectors in a way.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.850
The market about a decade ago

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.740
was softer than it is right now.

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:10.770
Back then, you could sell a
watch and get a return on it,

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.480
but you could also sell a Rolex

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.980
and it could have depreciated in value

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.390
and you could lose money on it.

00:02:15.390 --> 00:02:18.450
These days you now will likely
make more money off of it

00:02:18.450 --> 00:02:20.100
if you sell it on the resale market.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.350
- [Narrator] Much of the
success of the used watch market

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:25.530
is due to the rise of online
watch resale marketplaces

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:27.210
over the past decade.

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:30.416
That's where people like
Paul and Carol come in.

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.560
- (laughs) Can we hold that.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:32.700
- Get over there buddy.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.050
- [Narrator] The husband and wife duo

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.450
run Bob's Watches, an online marketplace

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.660
for buying, selling, and
trading luxury watches.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:40.980
They say that they currently have

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:42.270
one of the largest selections

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:44.910
of used Rolex watches in the world.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.860
- I started out in the watch business

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:51.060
because I could see that
there was no real safe,

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.850
transparent, honest place for people

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:55.560
to buy and sell pre-owned watches.

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.800
It's been an upward trend since 2010,

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.690
we've been growing consistently

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:03.570
about 30 to 40% year-over-year.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:07.380
Two years ago we did
$100 million in sales.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.960
- There's so much more for us to tap into

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.390
that we haven't had
the bandwidth to get to

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.420
because the growth has
been so fast and furious.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.030
- [Narrator] And Paul
and Carol love Rolex's.

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:19.890
Sales of used watches online

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.110
already exceed auction and store sales,

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:23.220
and one report predicts

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.320
they're going to reach close to 60%

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:28.470
of the secondhand luxury market by 2026.

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.360
- During the pandemic, the
stock market goes crazy.

00:03:30.360 --> 00:03:32.160
You have the kind of crypto phenomenon,

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.630
you have meme stocks happening,

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:35.490
and people have a lot of extra capital

00:03:35.490 --> 00:03:37.140
and they're taking that in many cases

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:39.060
and they're putting it toward assets,

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.670
luxury goods and in a
lot of cases watches.

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:43.020
- [Narrator] Starting in 2020,

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.630
used luxury watches sold for 1.5

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:47.820
to three times their retail prices.

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:49.530
- Rolex is a brand that's
really recognizable

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:52.050
in it's designed, it's, you
know easy to spot on the street.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:53.610
And a lot of people, they'll see that

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:54.780
their friend has a given Rolex,

00:03:54.780 --> 00:03:56.550
and they think, "I want that too."

00:03:56.550 --> 00:04:00.060
- But Rolex, the company,
only sold new watches,

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.110
which meant that the brand

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:03.450
wasn't involved with used watch sales,

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:06.150
that is until late 2022.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:08.610
Rolex opened a certified pre-owned program

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.110
for its used watches.

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:12.210
Retailers can send used Rolexes

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:15.240
that are at least three years
old back to the watchmaker.

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:16.920
The certified pre-owned program

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:19.350
verifies that a watch
is an authentic Rolex

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:20.730
and works properly,

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:22.830
then retailers can sell the watch

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:24.900
with an official Rolex certificate.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:26.340
The program is already active

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:29.130
in one retail chain in
six different countries.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:32.070
Another chain of official
Rolex retailers in the US

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:34.230
will enter the program this May.

00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:36.450
Buying a watch with Rolex certification

00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:38.820
could be a draw for first time buyers.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.320
- You're buying a watch on the internet,

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:42.330
it can be a little bit
of a daunting experience.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:44.610
- Of all the watches on our website today,

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:47.310
almost 50% of them already have

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.830
the original box and papers from Rolex.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:51.780
We've offered a CPO program,

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:54.390
a certified pre-owned program
now for almost five years.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.340
The only thing really new about it

00:04:56.340 --> 00:04:57.990
is that Rolex is certifying

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.490
and doing the paperwork behind it.

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:02.160
So I don't feel that there's
any increased competition,

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:05.010
but I do feel that the
market is big enough

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:06.720
for everybody to participate.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:08.940
- Today people buy Rolexes online

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.320
the way that they might buy toilet paper,

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.960
so it's really not a premium
or a specialized experience.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.070
There's still that consumer

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:16.020
that wants to have that
experience of going into a store,

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:18.450
of being waited on, of
kind of being shown watches

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:21.810
from a glass display case, and
making it feel more special

00:05:21.810 --> 00:05:23.880
because they're buying
something of such a high value.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.590
- [Narrator] This
certified pre-owned program

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:28.110
means that Rolex can take
a cut out of a market

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.150
that it previously left untapped,

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:31.920
but things might continue to shift

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:33.720
for the luxury watch market.

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:35.760
The used watch market is cooling down

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:37.620
as sellers eager to make a profit

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:39.930
have flooded the market with inventory.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:42.600
Recent data shows the
number of Rolex watches

00:05:42.600 --> 00:05:44.460
available to buy secondhand,

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:47.340
roughly doubled from the beginning of 2022

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.500
to September of the same year.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:52.350
- On those really coveted
kind of brand name watches,

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.180
so to speak, the ones
that collectors talk about

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:56.190
the resale value has
gone down a little bit.

00:05:56.190 --> 00:05:57.960
Resellers, people that watch that market,

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.270
they do say that the
prices have come back down

00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:03.180
to earth a little bit,
but the volume of sales,

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:04.560
the amount of sales happening

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:05.880
that still remains pretty high,

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.350
we're seeing still a large number

00:06:07.350 --> 00:06:08.850
of transactions in the resale market.

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:10.200
Your day-in, day-out Rolex

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.600
is still retaining a lot of
value on the resale market,

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.400
you can still get a
pretty good return for it.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:15.840
As with any resale market,

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:17.430
there is a risk that the Rolex market

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:18.870
can fall out at any time.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.520
Five years ago, we might
not have been talking about

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:21.510
how crazy this market is,

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:23.370
and five years from now we
might not be talking about

00:06:23.370 --> 00:06:24.720
how crazy this market is.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:25.890
The market is so large

00:06:25.890 --> 00:06:27.870
that to a certain extent
both things can be true.

00:06:27.870 --> 00:06:29.010
You know, people that watch this market

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:30.480
will say that that's just
actually a reflection

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:31.890
of how big the market is now,

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:33.870
where it can behave in many different ways

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:36.300
just because it is this
kind of really large

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:37.427
transactional marketplace.

00:06:37.427 --> 00:06:40.010
(upbeat music)

